[metadata]
project = "boj-server-cartridges"
version = "0.2.0"
last-updated = "2026-08-07"

@abstract:
Trust boundaries and integrity checks for boj-server-cartridges. Defines
what AI agents may do autonomously and what requires human approval, plus
checks that verify repository integrity.

Trust here is calibrated by BLAST RADIUS, not by file type. Since
hyperpolymath/boj-server#300 merged (2026-08-04) this repository is the sole
source of cartridges for every BoJ host, with no bundled fallback anywhere.
A bad merge to main reaches every host on its next fetch.
@end

## Trust Levels

The boj-server-cartridges repository operates at trust level: standard

Trust levels:
- maximal:    Agent may read, build, test, lint, format, heal freely.
              Only destructive/external actions require approval.
- standard:   Agent may read and build. Test/lint need approval.
- restricted: Agent may read only. All modifications need approval.
- minimal:    Agent may read specific files only. Everything else blocked.

Current trust level: standard

Rationale for standard rather than maximal: this repo has no bundled
fallback downstream, and several of its "green" signals are weaker than
they look (hypatia-scan is advisory; zig-test only sees ffi/ paths; nothing
builds the adapter layer). An agent that heals freely here can ship a
regression to every host without a single red check.

## Autonomous vs Approval

Autonomous (no approval needed):
- Read anything.
- Run the read-only gates: `deno task audit`, `bash scripts/check-trusted-base.sh`,
  `bash scripts/typecheck-proofs.sh`, `zig build test` inside a cartridge's ffi/.
- Edit a single cartridge's own docs, tests, or ffi/ sources.
- Recount and correct a number in .machine_readable/ when the recount
  command and result are shown.

Requires explicit approval:
- Any edit to schemas/cartridge-v1.json or schemas/PINNED-SHA.
- Any edit to cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/ — every future mint
  inherits it.
- Any batch edit spanning more than ~10 cartridges.
- Any change to .github/workflows/ that removes or weakens a gate.
- Any change to the TypeScript/AffineScript carve-out list.

## Integrity Invariants

### Secrets

#### no-secrets-committed
- description: No credential files in repo
- run: test ! -f .env && test ! -f credentials.json && test ! -f .env.local && test ! -f .env.production
- severity: critical

#### no-private-keys
- description: No private key files tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files | grep -E '\.(pem|key)$|(^|/)id_rsa$|(^|/)id_ed25519$')"
- severity: critical
- notes: Scoped to tracked files. A `find` over the working tree would trip over local build output and, worse, could pass or fail depending on untracked junk.

#### gitleaks-config-present
- description: The gitleaks configuration the secret-scanner relies on is in-tree
- run: test -f .gitleaks.toml
- severity: warning

### Supply Chain

#### schema-mirror-integrity
- description: The pinned schema mirror has not silently drifted
- run: test "$(sha256sum schemas/cartridge-v1.json | awk '{print $1}')" = "$(awk -F'"' '/content_sha256/ {print $2}' schemas/PINNED-SHA)"
- severity: critical

#### reusable-workflows-sha-pinned
- description: Every hyperpolymath reusable workflow call is pinned to a 40-char SHA, not a branch
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -z '.github/workflows/*.yml' | xargs -0 grep -ho 'uses: hyperpolymath/[^ ]*' | grep -v '@[0-9a-f]\{40\}$')"
- severity: critical
- notes: Scoped to TRACKED files, which is the surface CI actually runs. Passes 2026-08-07. Known adjacent risk, deliberately not hidden — the UNTRACKED file .github/workflows/main-estate-audit.yml, sitting in the working tree since before this branch, carries 26 hyperpolymath/cicd-suite action references all pinned to @main. If it is ever committed as-is this check turns red, which is the correct outcome. Commit it with SHA pins or delete it; do not weaken this check to accommodate it.

## Provenance

#### author-correct
- description: Git author matches expected identity
- run: git log -1 --format='%ae' | grep -qE '(hyperpolymath|j\.d\.a\.jewell|jonathan\.jewell)'
- severity: warning

#### commits-signed
- description: HEAD carries a valid signature
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: warning

#### license-content
- description: LICENSE contains the expected identifier
- run: grep -q 'MPL' LICENSE
- severity: warning
- notes: This repo is MPL-2.0. Docs (README.adoc, ADRs, cartridge READMEs) are CC-BY-SA-4.0. Never AGPL.

## Deny Areas

### trust-deny-areas
- description: Sensitive areas that require explicit approval before modification
- severity: advisory
- areas:
  - schemas/
  - cartridges/templates/gossamer-mcp/
  - .machine_readable/
  - 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
  - GOVERNANCE.md
  - MAINTAINERS.adoc
  - .github/CODEOWNERS
  - .github/workflows/
- notes: GOVERNANCE is .md in this repo. The previous version of this file listed GOVERNANCE.adoc, which commit c2da9ed removed.

## Container Security

#### no-dockerfile
- description: No Dockerfile (Containerfile is the estate convention)
- run: test ! -f Dockerfile
- severity: warning

#### container-images-pinned
- description: If a Containerfile appears, its base images must be pinned
- run: test ! -f Containerfile || grep -q 'cgr.dev\|@sha256:' Containerfile
- severity: warning
- notes: Vacuously true today — there is no Containerfile in this repository. Kept as a forward guard, and flagged as vacuous so nobody reads its green as evidence of a hardened image.
